    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Two dimensional flow equations for a slightly compressible fluid offer considerable promise for studying various aspects of reservoir fluid flow . Many types of phenomena can be simulated with this model. A rectangular grid was imposed on the reservoir. This kind of subdivision is generally adequate for representing most of a reservoir. However, difficulties arise in the neighborhood of a well. In order to better represent the presence of a well, in a reservoir, a modified two-dimensional radial flow treatment by Mrosovsky [7] was used. The model can be used to study single well problems, and can simulate pressure build-up, drawdown behavior and interference testing. The program can compute stream lines in a homogeneous, isotropic reservoir of any shape and with variable thickness. Any number of wells producing at variable flow rates at any location in the reservoir can be simulated.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
